[01:06.33]The bonfires burneth low along the coast
[01:14.00]The lanterns on the boats do gutter out
[01:21.05]The children sleep, the horn is set aside
[01:28.96]And the first cold wind of autumn moves about

[01:37.90]Haust kemr — the autumn it is coming
[01:45.55]The dark that we defied doth take the field
[01:52.43]The embers redden, blacken, fall to ash
[02:00.89]And the summer that we held we now must yield

[02:09.39]Deyjandi loginn! The dying flame!
[02:13.22]Goeth down, goeth down, along the shore!
[02:20.92]Heyr oss, Skogarmóðir — hear us, forest-mother!
[02:25.03]The summer that thou gavest is no more!
[02:32.71]Allt fýkr — all doth blow away!
[02:39.64]The light we raised, the night we made our own!
[02:47.54]We yield it back, we yield it to the dark
[02:55.95]And we standeth on the cold wet stone, alone!

[03:31.89]The last coal dieth grey upon the sand
[03:38.68]The sea goeth black beneath a starless sky
[03:46.65]And we who danced so bright but hours ago
[03:54.31]Do stand in silence — and we know not why we cry

[04:03.47]We yield the light
[04:07.05]We yield the long bright days
[04:11.17]We yield the summer back into the dark
[04:18.78]But hear us — hear us —

[04:23.28]Deyjandi loginn! The dying flame!
[04:26.65]Goeth down, goeth down, along the shore!
[04:34.63]Heyr oss, Skogarmóðir — hear us, forest-mother!
[04:38.71]The summer that thou gavest is no more!
[04:46.26]Allt fýkr — all doth blow away!
[04:53.49]The light we raised, the night we made our own!
[05:01.36]We yield it back, we yield it to the dark
[05:09.76]And we standeth on the cold wet stone, alone!

[05:20.04]But hear us —
